> how do you guard against the possibility that s/he may get subtly
> wrong results---no error messages---because of having version 1.2
> instead of version 2.1 of foobar.sty?

Well if foobar.sty defines a macro \foobarversion to be 1.2 (or 2.1)
you can test that. If not I suppose that if you know of a macro that
has changed in version 2.1, you can copy the definition of that to a
temp \cs, and test with \ifx against the macro defined by the style.

